# React patterns

Component design and anti-patterns for React 19-era code, narrowed to
`*.tsx`/`*.jsx`.

## Derive, don't sync

- Compute a value derivable from props/state during render (`useMemo` only when expensive); do not `useState` + `useEffect` to mirror one state into another.
- Reset local state on a prop change with a `key` tied to that prop, not an effect that calls a setter.
- Use effects only to synchronize with something outside React (DOM, subscription, network, browser storage, third-party widget); otherwise the logic belongs in an event handler or render.

## Lists and keys

- Give every `.map` element a stable `key` from the data (an id), not the array index, unless the list is provably static and never reordered/filtered/inserted into.
- Do not use `key` as a prop for anything but list identity; `props.key` is `undefined`.

## Forms and events

- Prefer a controlled input (`value` + `onChange`) when the component validates, transforms, or reacts as the user types; uncontrolled (`defaultValue` + ref) only for simple fields without per-keystroke reactivity.
- For submission with pending/error/optimistic state, prefer an Action (`<form action={...}>`, `useActionState`, `useOptimistic`) over hand-rolled `isSubmitting`/`error` state plus `preventDefault`.
- Use `useTransition` for non-urgent updates rather than hand-rolled debouncing or deferral.

## Refs, Suspense, and composition

- In React 19, `ref` is an ordinary prop: no `forwardRef` in new components; keep it only for code that must support pre-19 React.
- Read an async resource in render with `use` (promise or context) instead of an effect writing to state; pair with a `Suspense` boundary and an error boundary.
- Prefer composition (children, render props, focused components) over one component branching on a `type`/`variant` prop into unrelated trees.
- With server and client components, keep data fetching and secrets in server components; add `"use client"` only for a component that uses state, effects, refs, or browser-only APIs, not a whole subtree for one leaf.

## Compiler awareness

- With the React Compiler enabled (babel/swc config or `babel-plugin-react-compiler`/`react-compiler` dependency), do not hand-add `memo`, `useMemo`, or `useCallback` just to prevent re-renders. Without it, manual memoization is valid for a measured re-render cost.
